{
  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "TLS server identity verification in the production Go HTTPS client and Python MCP HTTPS opener. Real TLS over local memory/Unix socket pairs with isolated fixture trust and simulated DNS; no external servers or deployed routing.",
  "changes": [
    "Disable Python SSLContext.hostname_checks_common_name in the production opener. System trust, certificate verification, original hostname, TLS 1.2 minimum and HTTP/1.1 ALPN remain enabled.",
    "Refuse production Python opener creation when native Common Name exclusion is absent/false or OpenSSL predates 1.1.1l. This conservative runtime policy avoids historical flag behavior; it does not rely on older Python workarounds.",
    "No Go production change: its existing TLS verifier already rejected all denied identities.",
    "Add deterministic public certificate fixtures and shared handshake tests, including explicit certificate-verification error checks and no HTTP request delivery on denial. No Snort SID added."
  ],
