  "limitations": [
    "The explicit custom embedding opener and arbitrary caller-supplied TLS contexts are trusted integration hooks outside the production opener contract.",
    "The version gate is intentionally conservative: older native libraries are refused even where a particular Python release might work around their behavior. Old runtimes are simulated for startup checks, not executed.",
    "Fixtures test selected identity, trust, time and server-purpose outcomes. They are not complete PKIX, revocation, cipher, certificate-issuance, protocol or runtime vulnerability coverage.",
    "Generated keys are published test material. The fixture CA is loaded only into isolated test clients; no machine trust store is changed.",
    "TLS exchanges are local with fake DNS and numeric dial recording; there is no external-endpoint, sandbox perimeter or production deployment validation.",
    "Shared handshake cases are counted once across implementations. Baseline comparisons, repeated runs, certificate files and assertions are not additional cases.",
    "No universal RFC/W3C conformance or prevention of all unknown attacks is established."
  ],
